<deck title="ah-r showcase" />

# ah-r showcase

Code blocks, **live** shells, and real syntax highlighting — all in the
terminal.

Arrow keys to navigate, `q` to quit.

---

## A plain code block

An untagged fence renders as a styled (non-highlighted) block:

```
$ ah-r showcase.ahr-deck
rendering 11 slides…
```

---

## A live code block

A `<tty>` element runs a real command, streaming its output live:

<tty title="date, live" rows="6" cols="46">
while :; do date "+%H:%M:%S"; sleep 1; done
</tty>

---

## A persistent live block

This counter has `id="counter"` + `persist`, so it survives to the next slide:

<tty id="counter" persist title="counter" rows="8" cols="46">
i=0; while :; do echo "tick $i"; i=$((i + 1)); sleep 1; done
</tty>

---

## The same process, one slide later

It was **not** restarted — same `id`, so it kept counting:

<tty id="counter" persist title="counter" rows="8" cols="46">
i=0; while :; do echo "tick $i"; i=$((i + 1)); sleep 1; done
</tty>

---

## Rust, syntax highlighted

<code lang="rust">
use std::collections::HashMap;

fn main() {
    let mut counts: HashMap<&str, u32> = HashMap::new();
    for word in "a b a c b a".split_whitespace() {
        *counts.entry(word).or_insert(0) += 1;
    }
    println!("{counts:?}");
}
</code>

---

## HTML, syntax highlighted

<code lang="html">
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <body>
    <h1 class="title">ah-r</h1>
    <!-- a comment -->
    <p>Slides in your <strong>terminal</strong>.</p>
  </body>
</html>
</code>

---

## JavaScript, syntax highlighted

<code lang="js">
const slides = ["intro", "demo", "thanks"];

function present(deck) {
  return deck.map((name, i) => `${i + 1}. ${name}`).join("\n");
}

console.log(present(slides));
</code>

---

## Markdown, as highlighted source

<code lang="markdown">
# Heading

- a **bold** point
- a [link](https://example.com)

> a blockquote

`inline code` and a list above.
</code>

---

## Markdown, rendered

- a **bold** point and some *emphasis*
- a [link](https://example.com)
- `inline code`

> A blockquote, styled by the renderer.

1. first
2. second

